      "content": "‘Reddes are made .. of the red earth called Maiolica, otherwise browne of spaine’ (OED s.v. earth n. IV.17, quote of 1598); majolica is a red earth used as a pigment (OED s.v. majolica n. & adj. 1) | Pigment that is brown in color, does not contain carbon, and is ultimately not derived from vegetable or animal sources. [Source: Getty AAT]"
